#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/tilemap.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.tilemap.tilemap:31
msgid ""
"The bounding box of the map in the form of a list [*xmin*, *xmax*, *ymin*, "
"*ymax*]. These coordinates should be in longitude/latitude if "
"``lonlat=True`` or Spherical Mercator (EPSG:3857) if ``lonlat=False``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/tilemap.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.tilemap.tilemap:35
msgid ""
"Level of detail. Higher levels (e.g. ``22``) mean a zoom level closer to the "
"Earth's surface, with more tiles covering a smaller geographical area and "
"thus more detail. Lower levels (e.g. ``0``) mean a zoom level further from "
"the Earth's surface, with less tiles covering a larger geographical area and "
"thus less detail. Default is ``\"auto\"`` to automatically determine the "
"zoom level based on the bounding box region extent.  .. note::    The "
"maximum possible zoom level may be smaller than ``22``, and depends on    "
"what is supported by the chosen web tile provider source."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/tilemap.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.tilemap.tilemap:35
msgid ""
"Level of detail. Higher levels (e.g. ``22``) mean a zoom level closer to the "
"Earth's surface, with more tiles covering a smaller geographical area and "
"thus more detail. Lower levels (e.g. ``0``) mean a zoom level further from "
"the Earth's surface, with less tiles covering a larger geographical area and "
"thus less detail. Default is ``\"auto\"`` to automatically determine the "
"zoom level based on the bounding box region extent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/tilemap.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.tilemap.tilemap:43
msgid ""
"The maximum possible zoom level may be smaller than ``22``, and depends on "
"what is supported by the chosen web tile provider source."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/tilemap.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.tilemap.tilemap:46
msgid ""
"The tile source: web tile provider or path to a local file. Provide either:  "
"- A web tile provider in the form of a :class:`xyzservices.TileProvider` "
"object.   See :doc:`Contextily providers <contextily:providers_deepdive>` "
"for a list of   tile providers. Default is ``xyzservices.providers."
"OpenStreetMap.HOT``, i.e.   OpenStreetMap Humanitarian web tiles. - A web "
"tile provider in the form of a URL. The placeholders for the XYZ in the   "
"URL need to be ``{x}``, ``{y}``, ``{z}``, respectively. E.g.   ``https://{s}."
"tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png``. - A local file path. The file is "
"read with :doc:`rasterio <rasterio:index>` and   all bands are loaded into "
"the basemap. See   :doc:`contextily:working_with_local_files`.  .. "
"important::    Tiles are assumed to be in the Spherical Mercator projection "
"(EPSG:3857)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/tilemap.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.tilemap.tilemap:46
msgid ""
"The tile source: web tile provider or path to a local file. Provide either:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/tilemap.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.tilemap.tilemap:48
msgid ""
"A web tile provider in the form of a :class:`xyzservices.TileProvider` "
"object. See :doc:`Contextily providers <contextily:providers_deepdive>` for "
"a list of tile providers. Default is ``xyzservices.providers.OpenStreetMap."
"HOT``, i.e. OpenStreetMap Humanitarian web tiles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/tilemap.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.tilemap.tilemap:52
msgid ""
"A web tile provider in the form of a URL. The placeholders for the XYZ in "
"the URL need to be ``{x}``, ``{y}``, ``{z}``, respectively. E.g. ``https://"
"{s}.tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/tilemap.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.tilemap.tilemap:55
msgid ""
"A local file path. The file is read with :doc:`rasterio <rasterio:index>` "
"and all bands are loaded into the basemap. See :doc:`contextily:"
"working_with_local_files`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/tilemap.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.tilemap.tilemap:60
msgid ""
"Tiles are assumed to be in the Spherical Mercator projection (EPSG:3857)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/tilemap.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.tilemap.tilemap:62
msgid ""
"If ``False``, coordinates in ``region`` are assumed to be Spherical Mercator "
"as opposed to longitude/latitude."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/tilemap.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.tilemap.tilemap:65
msgid ""
"If the tile API is rate-limited, the number of seconds to wait between a "
"failed request and the next try."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/tilemap.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.tilemap.tilemap:68
msgid ""
"Total number of rejected requests allowed before contextily will stop trying "
"to fetch more tiles from a rate-limited API."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/tilemap.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.tilemap.tilemap:71
msgid ""
"The amount to adjust a chosen zoom level if it is chosen automatically. "
"Values outside of -1 to 1 are not recommended as they can lead to slow "
"execution."
msgstr ""

